## What this licence covers, and what it does not

The MIT terms above apply to this project's own code: everything under `src/`,
`test/`, `tools/`, `jni/jni.cpp`, `docker/`, the build scripts, and the documents
under `docs/`. Three things it does **not** cover:

- **The bundled font**, `assets/fonts/BetterTimelapseCjkSC-Regular.ttf`, is a subset
  of Sarasa Gothic and carries its own licence, which is included beside it
  (`assets/fonts/`). Sarasa Gothic is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and the
  font here is renamed as that licence requires of a modified version.
- **`jni/platform/`** is a git submodule pointing at
  [OpenMemories-Platform](https://github.com/ma1co/OpenMemories-Platform), which has
  its own licence. It is a build-time dependency and is not vendored into this
  repository.
- **The old app's behaviour**, analysed at length in `docs/PAIN-POINTS.md`, belongs
  to [TimeLapse](https://github.com/jonasjuffinger/TimeLapse). No code from it is
  used here: the analysis is of its behaviour and design, with file and line
  references, and the old app is not part of this repository.
